finding: P2: Invalid GPU row cull codes can alias valid declared pairs rather than draw nothing. src/standard/rendering/producer-table.ts:155 and src/standard/rendering/pack.ts:145 validate cullMode only after u32 multiplication by six; 0x80000000 * 6 wraps to zero, so both the guard and pair calculation treat that invalid code as Back. Independently reproduced on HEAD with a registered producer containing only a back-culled opaque StandardMaterial and cube: code 0 renders center [0,0,255,255], code 3 correctly gives clear [46,43,40,255], code 2147483648 incorrectly renders [0,0,255,255]. This violates MeshInstanceInput's documented above-2-draws-nothing contract and producer declared alpha/cull-pair validation. Validate the raw code before multiplication. The eight material-cull tests contain no malformed producer code and cannot catch this.
